      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>Yah Hatsel Yonah is a traditional piyyut for Ḥanukkah, of unknown origin (although it spells out the name Yehuda as an acrostic). Beloved in Iraqi Jewish circles, it discusses the hope that Israel, likened to a dove, will be able to celebrate Ḥanukkah during a time of true redemption. Included is a relatively literal (but de-gendered) translation, as well as a poetic singable one.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_48034_introduction"/>
